[Chapter "Early queen moves"]
[Line "Queen hits b7: 4.Qb3"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Mannheim Variation"]

{White attacks d5 and b7 with the queen. Black takes on c4 and develops with gain of time.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit: White attacks d5.} 2... c6 {The Slav: support d5 with a pawn and keep the c8 bishop's diagonal open, unlike ...e6.} 3. Nf3 Nf6 {Develop and guard d5 again.} 4. Qb3 {White hits d5 and eyes b7.} 4... dxc4 {Take: the queen must recapture, losing time.} 5. Qxc4 Bf5 {Bishop out before ...e6.} 6. Nc3 e6 {A solid chain, ready for ...Nbd7 and castling.} *
